</ul><p>Alternative cleaner: keep ONE pinned scrubbed timeline, but its first X% is "dead time" (nothing visible changes / the archery DOM overlays it). The archery interaction happens in real-time DOM-land (not scroll). Once the shot fires, I need scroll to "catch up" — e.g., the user has scrolled 30% into the pin while playing with the bow; after the shot, the tree sequence should start from its beginning — but scroll is already at 30%. Messy.</p><p>Cleanest: TWO-phase pin:</p><ul class="list-inside list-disc whitespace-normal" data-streamdown="unordered-list">
