 before:font-mono before:select-none"><span class="dark:bg-(--shiki-dark-bg)! dark:text-(--shiki-dark)!" style="color: rgb(36, 41, 46); --shiki-dark: #E1E4E8;">  </span><span class="dark:bg-(--shiki-dark-bg)! dark:text-(--shiki-dark)!" style="color: rgb(106, 115, 125); --shiki-dark: #6A737D;">// 5) outro: fade tree as we leave (blur like before)</span></span><span class="block before:content-[counter(line)] before:inline-block before:[counter-increment:line] before:w-4 before:mr-4 before:text-[13px] before:text-right before:text-muted-foreground/50 before:font-mono before:select-none"><span class="dark:bg-(--shiki-dark-bg)! dark:text-(--shiki-dark)!" style="color: rgb(36, 41, 46); --shiki-dark: #E1E4E8;">}</span></span><span class="block before:content-[counter(line)] before:inline-block before:[counter-increment:line] before:w-4 before:mr-4 before:text-[13px] before:text-right before:text-muted-foreground/50 before:font-mono before:select-none"></span></code></pre></div><p>Hmm — wait, the "hold" (scroll lock): the pin uses start "top top". When the section's top hits the viewport top, ScrollTrigger pins. I need to hold the user there until the shot fires. Mechanism: <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">ScrollTrigger.create({trigger: sec, start: "top top", onEnter: hold, onLeaveBack: releaseHold})</code> where hold(): if (!Archery.fired) { window.__lenis &amp;&amp; __lenis.stop(); show archery; start beat; arm autofire (wheel/touch/key → Archery.autoFire); timeout 9s → autoFire; cinemaHint check → autoFire soon }.</p><p>After fire: the shot timeline plays (~1.4s to burst + bloom), then: <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">window.__lenis &amp;&amp; __lenis.start()</code>.</p><p>Problem: with lenis stopped, native scroll can still occur via scrollbar drag or keyboard (Page Down). Then the pinned scrub timeline would advance before the shot fired. Mitigation: auto-fire on wheel/touch/key events (which covers most). Scrollbar drag — rare; also I can clamp: in the scrub timeline's onUpdate, if (!Archery.fired) scroll to pin start... too invasive. Acceptable: auto-fire covers wheel/touch/keys. Also without lenis (reduce motion), no lock — but reduce motion skips interaction anyway.</p><p>Hmm wait, actually there's a subtlety: <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">lenis.stop()</code> — during the hold, if the user scrolls with wheel, lenis is stopped so nothing happens, and I listen for wheel to auto-fire. After firing, lenis.start(). Good. Without lenis (reduced motion), the archery is skipped entirely: auto-fire instantly (or show final tree state).</p><p>What about entering the section from ABOVE going back down (scroll back up from road into corridor while fired already)? The shot is one-way (played=true). Scrolling back up: the scrub timeline runs in reverse — tree un-grows, camera pulls back... at progress 0 it shows... the post-bloom state? The archery overlay is gone (faded after burst). So scrolling back to pin start shows an empty night with the tree at growth 0 — hmm, that's a dead state. Options: (a) on reverse to start, re-arm archery (replay-able!); (b) at progress 0 keep a "resting tree" state (tree fully formed, no petals) so reverse scrolling shows the tree gently; (c) camera pull reveals the heart hanging again?</p><p>The Gift zip had a replay button. Simplest robust: keep the shot one-way, and make scrub progress 0 = "the tree world right after the bloom" (camera slightly outside, tree bare/small) growing to full bloom — reversing to 0 shows a small shimmering tree in the night — not dead, acceptable and actually nice (the tree breathes smaller/larger). Also re-arm on full reverse exit (onLeaveBack below pin start): if user scrolls back above the section and returns, reset the archery to play again? That's cute but adds state complexity (burst cleanup). Gift does resetAll. I'll implement Archery.reset() for re-entry when scrolled back ABOVE the section start (onLeaveBack of the hold trigger) — so re-entering replays the shot. That matches the "again" spirit. But careful with the scrub timeline (already at 0, fine) and Blossom state (setProgress(0)). Manageable: Archery.reset() rebuilds overlay states (gsap.set), Blossom.setProgress(0), fired=false, re-arm on re-pin. I'll implement reset carefully — moderate risk; if it flakes, one-way is the fallback. Actually... let me keep it simpler: re-arm ONLY when user fully leaves the section upward (onLeaveBack) AND the timeline is at 0. Since scrub reverse will be at 0 by then (pin releases when scrolled above start... wait, when pinned, scrolling back above start unpins and scrub = 0). Yes: onLeaveBack (scroll above pin start) → reset().</p><p>Edge: What if user force-scrolls (scrollbar) DURING hold to 50%? Then fired=false but scrub=0.5 (tree half-grown, weird since burst didn't happen — archery overlay still visible with bow+heart at 50% tree behind). Mitigate: also add a scroll listener during hold: if scrollY &gt; pinStart+40 while !fired → autoFire(). Good — covers scrollbar too.</p><p><span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong">Blossom module design</span> (js/blossom.js, ES module, window.Blossom):</p><div class="my-4 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border" data-language="js" data-streamdown="code-block" style="content-visibility: auto; contain-intrinsic-size: auto 200px;"><div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-muted/80 p-3 text-muted-foreground text-xs" data-language="js" data-streamdown="code-block-header"><span class="ml-1 font-mono lowercase">js</span><div class="flex items-center gap-2"><button class="cursor-pointer p-1 text-muted-foreground transition-all hover:text-foreground disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50" data-streamdown="code-block-download-button" title="Download file" type="button"><svg xmlns="http