down="inline-code">mat.defines = { "USE_UV": "" }</code> — for r160 MeshBasicMaterial with uv... CircleGeometry has uv attribute; USE_UV define — in r160 the define name for basic materials... r160 uses <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">USE_UV</code> when map present; setting defines manually works (the shader declares varying vUv under <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">#ifdef USE_UV</code>). In r160, <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">uv_pars_vertex</code> chunk: <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">#if defined( USE_UV ) || defined( USE_ANISOTROPY )</code> — vUv declared. Fragment <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">uv_pars_fragment</code> similar. ✓ works.</p><p>Another check — <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">#include &lt;opaque_fragment&gt;</code> exists in r160 meshbasic fragment ✓ (renamed from output_fragment in r154).</p><p>Points shader: <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">gl_PointSize = size;</code> — exact string in r160 points_vert ✓.</p><p><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">vec4 diffuseColor = vec4( diffuse, opacity );</code> — exact in r160 points_frag ✓.</p><p><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">#include &lt;clipping_planes_fragment&gt;</code> in points_frag ✓ (it's in meshphysical and points too — points_frag has clipping_planes_fragment at the end ✓).</p><p><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">#include &lt;begin_vertex&gt;</code> ✓.</p><p>texture2D on WebGL2: three prepends <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">#define texture2D texture</code> for WebGL2? Actually three converts GLSL1 built-in shaders appropriately — in WebGL2, three still compiles shaders as GLSL ES 1.00 by default (no #version 300 es) unless material.glslVersion === GLSL3. So texture2D valid ✓.</p><p>Hmm — one more: petal vertex shader replace of <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">gl_PointSize = size;</code> — my replacement references <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">isEffect</code> — declared above in the begin_vertex replace block (local float in main) ✓ since begin_vertex comes before gl_PointSize assignment in points_vert? Order in points_vert r160:</p><div class="my-4 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border" data-language="" data-streamdown="code-block" style="content-visibility: auto; contain-intrinsic-size: auto 200px;"><div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-muted/80 p-3 text-muted-foreground text-xs" data-language="" data-streamdown="code-block-header"><span class="ml-1 font-mono lowercase"></span><div class="flex items-center gap-2"><button class="cursor-pointer p-1 text-muted-foreground transition-all hover:text-foreground disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50" data-streamdown="code-block-download-button" title="Download file" type="button"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-download" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 15V3"></path><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"></path><path d="m7 10 5 5 5-5"></path></svg></button><button class="cursor-pointer p-1 text-muted-foreground transition-all hover:text-foreground disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50" data-streamdown="code-bloc