rt. Hmm — inconsistent freeze points → smells like a RACE: something happens at a TIME, not a scroll position! Both animations froze ~1.4-1.9s after start...</p><p>TIME-BASED! What happens ~1.2-2s after my scrollTo? <span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong">THE HOUSE MOUNTS!</span> main.js: <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">window.__bdayReady = true; dispatchEvent('bday:ready')</code> at build() — that's ~at gate open (build ran before gate). boot-house.js boots on bday:ready → mountHouse() → then <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">ScrollTrigger.refresh()</code>. Hmm — that all happened BEFORE my scrolls (gate click → 1.2s wait → scroll). House mounted at build, before gate click even. Hmm.__</p><p>BUT — <span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong">the HOUSE has a trigger-position repair pass on every refresh</span> AND the house pin spacer = 11200px. When did the house mount relative to my measurement of corrTop? corrTop=10300 measured AFTER gate. House spacer already in layout at measurement ✓ (pins dump shows house 20000→31200 ✓).</p><p>What about <span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong"><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">gsap.ticker.lagSmoothing(0)</code></span> + heavy first render of house (WebGL) — a long frame during my scroll animation → lenis animate.advance with huge dt → jumps?... The lenis raf is <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">gsap.ticker.add(t =&gt; lenis.raf(t * 1000))</code> — during a long GSAP frame, t jumps → advance(0.001<em>dt) — animate's internal time-based easing — a big dt just advances further — not freeze.</em></p><p>FREEZE with target=anim=y=5401 — the animation ENDED at 5401 (target was RETARGETED to 5401!). Who retargets? A native scroll event (onNativeScroll syncs target=actual=animated). So a NATIVE scroll to 5401 occurred — i.e., <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">window.scrollTo(0, 5401)</code> or scrollTop assignment or... <span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong">ScrollTrigger's internal <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">_scrollTo</code> during pinning/refresh!</span> ScrollTrigger does manipulate scroll when pinning with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">pinSpacing</code> on refresh to compensate._</p><p><span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong">OR THE SMOKING GUN: <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">ScrollTrigger.refresh()</code> — the HOUSE module's repair pass runs on EVERY refresh — and something refreshes during scroll: <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">main.js</code> resize listener (no resize here)... <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">visibilitychange</code>... OR ScrollTrigger's OWN refresh on pin toggle? NO...</span></p><p>Hmm wait — <span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong"><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">boot-house.js</code>: <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">ScrollTrigger.addEventListener("refresh", repairTriggerPositions)</code></span> — repairTriggerPositions calls <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">t.refresh()</code> on EVERY trigger — INDIVIDUAL refresh calls... <span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong"><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">ScrollTrigger</code>'s instance <code class="rounded bg-