amdown="strong">World.setScroll listener</span> — passive, reads only.</p><p>WAIT — <span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong"><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">parallax.js</code>!</span> Let me look at what parallax.js does — the #parallax scene is 0→6000 — 5401 and 6040 are both INSIDE/NEAR the parallax section!! The parallax scene has <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">#pxScroll</code> "scrollElement" — and parallax.js might create triggers with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">onUpdate</code> that do <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">window.scrollTo</code> or <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">lenis.scrollTo</code> — e.g., a "scroll snap to the arrival title"... Let me READ parallax.js fully! It's 10K. There could be a <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">snap</code> or an onEnter that scrolls. THAT would explain freeze points inside the parallax section (5401, 6040 within 0-6000... 6040 slightly past). Actually parallax section: 0→6000 (years top 6000). 6040 is 40px INTO the years section (before years pin start? years pin starts at 6000 = years top — so 6040 is inside years pin range!). Hmm but 5401 is inside parallax.</p><p>Let me just read parallax.js.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="prose prose-pre:bg-transparent prose-pre:p-0 text-wrap break-words prose-base body-base"><p>Freeze points parallax/years boundary ke aas-paas hain. <code class="rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-surface-tertiary font-mono text-[0.9em] text-text-primary font-medium" node="[object Object]">parallax.js</code> poora padhta hoon — kahin scroll manipulate toh nahi kar raha:</p></div><div><button type="button" aria-expanded="fal