reak). So presenting the zip is right, and the live preview server for actual browsing.</p><p>Let me curl-check the server, then present.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div><button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Expand" class="flex w-full select-none items-center gap-1.5 cursor-pointer"><svg width="1.5em" height="1.5em" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" color="currentColor" class="text-text-tertiary size-4 shrink-0"><path d="M13 16H18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M6 8L10 12L6 16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M2 18V6C2 4.89543 2.89543 4 4 4H20C21.1046 4 22 4.89543 22 6V18C22 19.1046 21.1046 20 20 20H4C2.89543 20 2 19.1046 2 18Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg><span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1"><span class="text-text-tertiary body-sm leading-4">used</span><span class="text-text-secondary body-sm leading-4">Bash</span><svg width="1.5em" height="1.5em" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" color="currentColor" class="text-interactive-positive size-4 shrink-0"><path d="M5 13L9 17L19 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg><span class="text-text-tertiary shrink-0 font-mono text-[10px] leading-[1.2]">329ms</span></span><svg width="1.5em" height="1.5em" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" color="currentColor" class="text-text-tertiary size-3 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="M6 9L12 15L18 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></button></div><div class="prose prose-pre:bg-transparent prose-pre:p-0 text-wrap break-words prose-base body-base"><p>Ho gaya bhai! 🏹🌸 <strong>Scene 2 (Memories corridor) ab "The Shot" hai</strong> — Gift zip ka bow-arrow intro + Blossom zip ka 3D WebGL tree, bilkul jaisa tumne bola tha.</p><h2>Naya Scene II — kaise chalta hai</h2><ol>
<li><strong>Bow &amp; arrow intro</strong> (Gift zip se) — pin hote hi scroll rukta hai, night sky ke saamne dil dhadakta hai aur neeche-left mein recurve bow. String kheencho (drag / Enter / Space) → arrow udta hai → dil phatta hai → mini-hearts burst + rose wash</li>
<li><strong>Gold bloom → 3D tree</strong> (Blossom zip se) — washes ke peeche WebGL blossom tree khada hai, site ke apne night sky ke neeche (transparent renderer)</li>
<li><strong>Scroll = camera orbit</strong> — tree bloom hota hai, 15,000 petals upar spiral karte hain, <strong>"2026" gold petals mein mid-air banta hai</strong> (years theme se perfect match!), phir wish: <em>"and the wish took root / Happy Birthday, Dipin. / here's to a year that blooms"</em> → phir road/celebration/house sab pehle jaisa</li>
</ol><h2>Technical jo maine handle kiya</h2><ul>
<li><strong>three.js r160 port</strong> — OrbitControls hata kar scroll-driven camera + mouse parallax; <code class="rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-surface-tertiary font-mono text-[0.9em] text-text-primary font-medium" node="[object Object]">tree.obj</code> project ke andar vendor kar diya (koi external dependency nahi, procedural fallback bhi hai)</li>
<li><strong>Saare fallbacks</strong>: 9s baad auto-fire (agar koi shoot na kare — lekin string pakde ho toh interrupt nahi karta), cinema mode kabhi wait nahi karta, reduced-motion mein seedha tree, no-WebGL par wish phir bhi land hoti hai, aur wapas scroll karne par <strong>bow re-arm ho jata hai</strong></li>
<li>Existing live score continue hota hai + burst par <code class="rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-surface-tertiary font-mono text-[0.9em] text-text-primary font-medium" node="[object Object]">pop()</code>, wish par <code class="rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-surface-tertiary font-mono text-[0.9em] text-text-primary font-medium" node="[object Object]">chime()</code></li>
