t position._</p><p>Hmm, let me look at this from a different angle — maybe scrollTo DID work and scrollY 12014 is... 0.465<em>3900+10300 = 12113.5 — 12014 ≠ 12113. And target 12618. Neither. Hmm 12014 = ? 0.437</em>3900+10300. Guided destination: GATE 0.345 → hold at scrollY 10314+... wait the hold: scroll was at 10314 (0.345 ≈ 1345 → 10300+1345 = 11645?? no wait. GATE = 0.34 → gate scroll = 10300 + 1326 = 11626. I jumped to 0.345 → 10300+1345=11645. Hmm — but the hold clamps scroll? No — hold stops lenis; native scroll jump to 11645 (past gate 11626 by 19px) — then hold's gate check <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">scrollY &gt; gateY + 90</code>? 11645 &lt; 11716 → normal hold path ✓. Then autoFire → onBloom: lenis.scrollTo(scrollY + TOTAL*0.12) = 11645+468 = 12113, duration 1.6. Lands 12113. Then my jump to 12618 at 6s... scrollY read 12014?!</p><p>12014 &lt; 12113. Something scrolled BACK by ~100px. OH — maybe the <span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong">scrub timeline's <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">immediateRender</code>/pin recalculation</span> — a ScrollTrigger.refresh() mid-flight recalculating pin positions and... no, doesn't move scroll.</p><p>Hmm — actually, wait: <span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong">Lenis's smoothWheel isn't involved, but lenis v1.1.13 has "lerp" mode</span>: onNativeScroll adopts native position INTO lenis target — then lenis's raf... <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">animate.advance</code> — if <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">isScrolling</code> was 'native'... Actually there's a known lenis behavior: after native scroll, lenis may continue "smooth scrolling" toward its own target if it thinks a scroll is in progress (velocity). The <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 p