ne has few objects? no — full scene with 4200+2500 points every frame always = battery drain). Compromise: when NOT active, still render ONE clear frame then stop... but the black compositing can recur anytime... Actually the standard fix: when inactive, call <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">renderer.clear()</code> once and ALSO set <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">canvas.style.opacity = 0</code> handled by tl anyway... Hmm.</p><p>Better robust approach: <span class="font-semibold" data-streamdown="strong">render at low cadence when inactive</span> (every ~500ms clear+render) — keeps the buffer fresh, negligible cost. OR: only render when the canvas element is actually on-screen/visible (IntersectionObserver on canvas within corridor pin + opacity&gt;0 check). Let me do: loop always runs; each frame:</p><ul class="list-inside list-disc whitespace-normal" data-streamdown="unordered-list">
