inline-code">enter()</code> gate click — gate shown after finishLoad ✓.</p><p>One more consideration: previously <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">build()</code> was called on DOM ready quickly; now the same. The gate opening is delayed until house+tree ready — that's the requested behavior ("bar full only when page fully ready to scroll").</p><p>Edge: if Blossom module fails to LOAD (script error) — <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">window.Blossom</code> undefined → pollUntil times out at 7000 → resolves → stage.tree=1 ✓.</p><p>Now — also there's the earlier <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">setTimeout(build, 5000);</code> hard timeout — I removed it (replaced by stage timeouts) ✓ (build is inside the ready chain with its own caps).</p><p>Next: remaining ideas integration check:</p><ul class="list-inside list-disc whitespace-normal" data-streamdown="unordered-list">
