ed px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">r &gt; 170 &amp;&amp; b &gt; g &amp;&amp; b &gt; r * 0.4 &amp;&amp; g &gt; r * 0.22</code>.</p><p>Sakura colors: inner (1.0, 0.88, 0.91) → at full brightness (255, 224, 232): b(232) &gt; g(224) ✓, b &gt; r<em>0.4 ✓, g &gt; r</em>0.22 ✓ → detected. Outer (0.94, 0.45, 0.60) → (240, 115, 153): b&gt;g ✓ ✓ ✓ → detected.</p><p>So why fewer pink pixels? Possibly this run the screenshot was at a different moment/scene state? grow=0.963, progress 0.444 — similar to before. Hmm — earlier successful pink run: "pink 1.44%" with dark 53%. Now dark only 25.4% — the screen is brighter — the WASH? Wait — the gold wash/bloom covers... at 0.444 with wash gone... Hmm — actually maybe the screenshot caught the shot-wish/bwGlow state, or the moon+halo covering more.</p><p>Wait — pixproof jumps to pin.len*0.62 — progress 0.444 hmm earlier also 0.444 with 1.44% pink. The difference: dark 25% vs 53% — something big and bright covers the screen. The HALO is bigger now (40×40 at alpha 0.46 — was already 40×40 @ 0.40 → slight). The moon? Both runs had moon. The AURA rim (1.10 scale, additive 0.11)?? That's along the tree silhouette — adds brightness.</p><p>Hold on — one important thing: my pink detector requires <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm" data-streamdown="inline-code">b &gt; g</code>. Sakura INNER (255,224,232): b=232 &gt; g=224 ✓ barely. But the blend with vDim darkening and alpha compositing over dark background: a pink blossom at alpha 0.5 over dark bg (10,6,12) → (132, 115, 122): b&gt;g ✓, r&gt;170? NO — 132 &lt; 170! The r&gt;170 threshold kills dimmed/semi-transparent blossoms! With vDim (depth cue) many blossoms are dimmed (0.35-1.0 factor) → r drops below 170.</p><p>But that was true before too... before: 1.44% — colors were inner (1.0,0.80,0.84)=(255,204,214) &amp; outer (0.95,0.42,0.55)=(242,107,140). Similar. Hmm — what made pink count DROP?</p><p>OH WAIT. I bet it's the alpha chan